Design a VESA adapter plate in OpenSCAD: a flat plate 7.2 mm thick carrying a 96.7 by 96.7 mm square bolt pattern and a 103.6 by 103.6 mm square bolt pattern, with 4.3 mm holes, to adapt one VESA mount to another.

This is the OpenSCAD file I wrote:
```openscad
// VESA adapter plate - a flat plate carrying two square bolt patterns, to mount a display
// or bracket drilled for one VESA size onto another. NOVEL general mount.
//

src   = 96.7;
dst   = 103.6;
thick = 7.2;
hole  = 4.3;

$fn = 48

size = max(src, dst) + 2 * hole + 12;

difference() {
    translate([-size / 2, -size / 2, 0]) cube([size, size, thick]);
    for (p = [src, dst])
        for (x = [-p / 2, p / 2])
            for (y = [-p / 2, p / 2])
                translate([x, y, -1]) cylinder(h = thick + 2, d = hole);
}
```

